---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii2_84",
  "series": "Band II 2 (1686 - 1694)",
  "seq": 84,
  "text": "<p> [[343.9]] <b>85. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS</p>\n<p> [[343.10]] Hannover, [18.] September 1690. [81.98.]</b></p>\n<p> [[343.20]] Nobilissime <Fn><i>Am Kopf der Seite von Leibniz' Hand</i>: Ad Dn. Vincentium Placcium Hamburgum Septemb. 1690</Fn> et Ampl^#'m^#'e Vir, Fautor Honoratissime </p>\n<p> [[343.21]] Valere Te ex sententia, et mei meminisse peramanter ex literis tuis intelligere gratissimum\n[[343.22]] fuit. Quanto enim pauciores sunt, qui sincero studio ad veritatem contendunt, eamque animi\n[[343.23]] facultatem divinitus accepere, ut praestare aliquid possint, profuturum posteris, eo magis\n[[343.24]] complecti eos, et si fieri possit, adjuvare decet. Itaque, si quid possum (quod quam exiguum sit\n[[344.1]] non diffiteor) id omne promtum jussis tuis offero. Vicissim hoc a Te spondeo mihi. Gaudeo\n[[344.2]] quod Cryptonymorum detegendorum consilium urges, insigni haud dubie rei literariae accessione;\n[[344.3]] cujus pars non contemnenda consistit in notitia scriptorum. Scio esse qui omnem illam\n[[344.4]] curiositatem inutilem judicent, quasi rerum non scriptorum habenda sit ratio. Sed hi non vident\n[[344.5]] in tanta multitudine rerum cognoscendarum, ingentis compendii esse, aliorum frui laboribus.\n[[344.6]] Itaque necessaria librorum notitia est, libros autem plerumque commendat autor, facileque\n[[344.7]] intelligitur, quod ab insigni viro scriptum est utiliter legi. </p>\n<p> [[344.8]] Sed majoris longe momenti esse fateor consilium Tuum <i>Ethices</i>, id est Medicinae Animi\n[[344.9]] tradendae, ad exemplum Medicinae Corporis. Non dubito quin legeris quae Tschirnhusius meus\n[[344.10]] dedit de <i>Medicina mentis et corporis</i>. Jam olim Parisiis familiaris inter nos notitia fuit (: fassusque <Fn>(: fassusque\n[[344.11]] ... dedit :): <i>Diese Passage hat Leibniz in eckige Klammern gesetzt, wohl um sie von der Abfertigung auszuschließen.</i></Fn> ipse est tunc potissimum profecisse. Itaque magna pars eorum quae tradit sententiis\n[[344.12]] meis consonat. Sunt tamen aliqua in quibus non assentior, quae admonuissem, si de edendi libri\n[[344.13]] consilio mihi constitisset. Notavi enim quaedam ipsi (ut solet contingere ingeniosis) visa fuisse\n[[344.14]] faciliora, a quibus tamen longe adhuc absunt quae dedit :). Cartesio olim haerebat pressius,\n[[344.15]] argumentoque ab ideis nimium tribuebat, quasi omnia de quibus loqui intelligibiliter licet, sub\n[[344.16]] ideam cadant. Verum a me ostensum est, ejus demum notionis ideam haberi, quam possibilem\n[[344.17]] esse demonstratum est cui doctrinae ille postea bonam partem suorum superstruxit. Caeterum\n[[344.18]] illi Medicina intellectus potissimum curae fuit, tibi, opinor proposita est Medicina Voluntatis. </p>\n<p> [[344.19]] Quis ille candidatus juris, qui in Anonymis ordinandis operam praestitit sed nunc alio\n[[344.20]] abit? Vellem egomet aliquando reperire adolescentem magnae spei, qui [et jam tum ingenio]\n[[344.21]] styloque valeat, et ardore discendi late patente ad majora contendat, sed quem res angusta domi\n[[344.22]] cogat ad alienam opem confugere. </p>\n<p> [[345.1]] Accepi nuper missum ab amico libellum cui titulus est: <i>Exercitatio theoricorum mathematico-physico-theologicorum</i>,\n[[345.2]] rei planetariae tradendae inservientem qui C^#'l^#'m^#'o Zimmermanno\n[[345.3]] viro docto apud vos nunc agenti olim Wurtenbergici agri parocho tribuitur. Is magno et\n[[345.4]] laudabili ardore videtur ad inquisitionem veritatis contendere, eoque dignum se praestare\n[[345.5]] bonorum amicitia. Agnosco multos homines pios, ut Henricum Morum, et ipsum cl. Zimmermannum\n[[345.6]] (ambos <greek>kabbalistikvtéroyw</greek>) abhorrere a philosophia Mechanica hoc est a ratione\n[[345.7]] Mathematica explicandi phaenomena naturae. Indignum enim putant Majestate Universi, omnia\n[[345.8]] velut in officina artificis fieri et verentur ne spirituales substantiae excludantur (quorsum fateor\n[[345.9]] nonnulli ex Corpusculariis tendunt) quo nihil potest esse a pietate alienius. Sed si satis explorata\n[[345.10]] essent optimis viris, quae a me in hoc argumento sunt demonstrata, in gratiam fortasse\n[[345.11]] redirent cum intelligibili philosophia. Ostendi enim etsi omnia phaenomena naturae corporeae\n[[345.12]] specialia possint explicari Mechanice seu ex corporum legibus, ipsa tamen prima Mechanices\n[[345.13]] principia, seu Leges motus Generales, oriri a causa incorporea nec per solam Mathesin sed per\n[[345.14]] Metaphysicam explicari debere. Neque absurdum mihi videtur quod illi asserunt non in nobis\n[[346.1]] tantum sed et passim in aliis rebus aliquid vitale reperiri. Attamen in explicandis phaenomenis\n[[346.2]] corporum specialibus non magis vita atque anima aut facultatibus incorporeis utendum censeo,\n[[346.3]] quam anima rationali ad explicandam humani corporis oeconomiam. (: Corpus <Fn>(: Corpus ... coaptentur.): <i>Diese Passage hat Leibniz in eckige Klammern gesetzt, wohl um sie von der Abfertigung auszuschließen.</i></Fn> pariter atque\n[[346.4]] anima suas sibi proprias habent leges, quae ab actione alterius non violantur, neque id vero\n[[346.5]] opus est, cum sponte naturae summo consensu sibi invicem coaptentur. :) Miror impense\n[[346.6]] Morum et Zimmermannum omnem gravitatis et Elastri Mechanicam explicationem rejicere.\n[[346.7]] Quasi deessent Deo rationes efficiendi talia per motuum leges. Cum admisso etiam Hylarchico\n[[346.8]] principio (quod nec omnino rejecerim) constare sibi nihilominus debeant corporeae rationes.\n[[346.9]] Quod si vir ingeniosissimus considerasset ante biennium <i>de Motuum coelestium</i> <i>causis</i>, edita in\n[[346.10]] <i>Actis</i> Lipsiensibus 1689, credo a vorticibus materiae aethereae minus esset alienus et fortasse\n[[346.11]] adjutor nobis foret egregius ad physicam coelestem perficiendam. Hoc ideo scribo, ut si forte\n[[346.12]] nosti virum, aut noscendi occasiones habes, materiam ipsi praebeas de his cogitandi uberius ne\n[[346.13]] praejudiciis quibusdam ipse viam sibi praecludat ad pulcherrimas veritates. </p>\n<p> [[346.14]] Ecce aliud non dissimile quod a Te postulare audeo. Vidi nuper libellum Germanicum de\n[[346.15]] Numerorum problematibus, ex quo intelligo Hamburgi Arithmeticos quosdam praestantiores\n[[347.1]] coivisse in societatem, aliis ex vicino in idem consilium ascitis, et Meisnerum quendam\n[[347.2]] vestratem artis magistrum (in schola ad D. Jacobi), esse autorem instituti. Perplacuit consilium,\n[[347.3]] et inde aliquid egregii nobis promitto, si velint operam ad ea conferre, quibus pomoeria\n[[347.4]] scientiae proferantur. Nam peculiaribus problematibus quando vel singularis elegantiae utilitatisque\n[[347.5]] non sunt, vel non faciunt ad ipsam Methodum Generalem longius promovendam,\n[[347.6]] tempus teri non satis dignum est tanto conatu. Nihil facilius est quam concinnare problemata\n[[347.7]] quae nobis originem noscentibus in promtu sunt, aliis vero majus negotium necessario facessunt.\n[[347.8]] Cogitandum igitur est de Analysi ipsa perficienda, neque arbitror quenquam nunc esse in\n[[347.9]] Germania, qui majore quam ego studio (ne dicam successu, id enim pro parte fortunae est) in eo\n[[347.10]] genere sit versatus. Habemus equidem dudum Methodum Generalem pro resolvendis aequationibus\n[[347.11]] cubicis; nam difficultatem quae nascitur cum radix quadratica extrahenda est ex falsa\n[[347.12]] quantitate non moror, nec pro impedimento habeo; et Methodum etiam generalem habemus\n[[347.13]] resolvendi aequationes quadrato-quadraticas seu quarti gradus. Nunc superest, ut etiam similes\n[[347.14]] Methodi pro altioribus gradibus reperiantur. Hactenus enim quantum constat non sunt in\n[[347.15]] artificum potestate. Quam in rem inventa quaedam dare possem late patentia, si vacaret ipsos\n[[347.16]] calculos absolvere. Habeo et inventum condendi Tabulas quasdam Algebraicas, quae si semel\n[[347.17]] darentur mirifice calculum sublevarent, et prope tantum utilitatis praestarent in Analysi, quantum\n[[347.18]] Tabulae sinuum vel Logarithmorum in numeris communibus. His elaborandis si quid\n[[347.19]] conferret societas communi bono socii primum prae aliis frui possent. Quodsi viri isti revera\n[[347.20]] amore augendae scientiae ducuntur, sperarem accedente ipsorum opera praestari aliquid posse\n[[347.21]] in Germania, quod longe omnia hactenus in Algebra inventa supergrediatur. Tu vero statues,\n[[348.1]] Vir Cl^#'m^#'e an Tibi cum Meisnero illo colloqui vacet, ejusque et per ipsum collegarum studium\n[[348.2]] excitare ad res praeclaras, sed nomine meo adhuc dissimulato. Haec non alteri facile scriberem,\n[[348.3]] sed cum Te sciam intelligere, quanti sit conferre ad Augmenta scientiarum, ex meo ingenio\n[[348.4]] judico non tantum non ingratas sed etiam jucundas tibi esse occasiones de re publica bene\n[[348.5]] merendi. Vale. </p>\n",
  "number": "85.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS",
  "date": "Hannover, [18.] September 1690. [81.98.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:85. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS Hannover, [18.] September 1690. [81.98.] Nobilissime Am Kopf der Seite von Leibniz' Hand: Ad Dn. Vincentium Placcium Hamburgum Septemb. 1690 et Ampl^#'m^#'e Vir, Fautor Honoratissime Valere Te ex sententia, et mei meminisse peramanter ex literis tuis intelligere grati...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>